    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d109">

                <pb facs="0240" n="150" xml:id="pg150"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.00/2284: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-12-27T17:00:00-04:40"><hi rendition="#italic">December 27,
                                1920—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received December 28—3
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>57. The issuing of the proclamation last Thursday<anchor n="22" xml:id="d109-f1"
                    /> has produced epidemic of protest in the press which is controlled by
                    politicians. National Committee circulating protest declaring that nothing but
                    abrogating and immediate restitution of sovereignty will be acceptable to the
                    Dominican people. In view of the attitude of the press it may be difficult to
                    secure Dominicans for the Commission.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
